AVP Narration: of the NETS service contracting program

asr-000351
00:43:34.840 --> 00:43:37.840
AVP Narration: in Araneta Center Bus Terminal in Quezon City

asr-000352
00:43:37.840 --> 00:43:39.580
AVP Narration: and the fuel subsidy program

asr-000353
00:43:39.580 --> 00:43:42.080
AVP Narration: in Paranaque Integrated Terminal Exchange.

asr-000354
00:43:42.080 --> 00:43:43.960
AVP Narration: The DOTR likewise continues to improve

asr-000355
00:43:43.960 --> 00:43:45.960
AVP Narration: to implement a 50% fair discount

asr-000356
00:43:45.960 --> 00:43:48.960
AVP Narration: to all passengers with MRT3 and LRT2.

asr-000357
00:43:48.960 --> 00:43:53.040
AVP Narration: In the railway sector,

asr-000358
00:43:53.040 --> 00:43:55.040
AVP Narration: the DOTR is splitting up the construction

asr-000359
00:43:55.040 --> 00:43:57.540
AVP Narration: of mass transit railway systems.

asr-000360
00:43:57.540 --> 00:44:00.540
AVP Narration: One of the biggest is the Metro Manila Subway Project,

asr-000361
00:44:00.540 --> 00:44:02.540
AVP Narration: which is fast taking shape underground

asr-000362
00:44:02.540 --> 00:44:04.540
AVP Narration: from Valenzuela to Naia.

asr-000363
00:44:04.540 --> 00:44:06.540
AVP Narration: Once operational,

asr-000364
00:44:06.540 --> 00:44:10.540
AVP Narration: the 33-kilometer, 17-station Metro Manila Subway Project

asr-000365
00:44:10.540 --> 00:44:13.540
AVP Narration: which will run from Valenzuela City to Naia

asr-000366
00:44:13.540 --> 00:44:15.040
AVP Narration: will reduce travel time from 90 minutes

asr-000367
00:44:15.040 --> 00:44:17.040
AVP Narration: to just 41 minutes

asr-000368
00:44:17.040 --> 00:44:21.040
AVP Narration: and will benefit around 519,000 passengers daily.

asr-000369
00:44:21.040 --> 00:44:22.040
AVP Narration: Last February,

asr-000370
00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:24.040
AVP Narration: President Ferdinand Marcus Jr.

asr-000371
00:44:24.040 --> 00:44:26.040
AVP Narration: led the groundbreaking ceremony

asr-000372
00:44:26.040 --> 00:44:28.040
AVP Narration: of two underground stations and tunnels

asr-000373
00:44:28.040 --> 00:44:30.040
AVP Narration: for the Bonifacio Global City

asr-000374
00:44:30.040 --> 00:44:32.040
AVP Narration: and Kalayaan Avenue Station.

asr-000375
00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:34.040
AVP Narration: It will serve about 200,000 passengers

asr-000376
00:44:34.040 --> 00:44:36.040
AVP Narration: in its opening year.

asr-000377
00:44:36.040 --> 00:44:37.040
AVP Narration: On the other hand,

asr-000378
00:44:37.040 --> 00:44:40.040
AVP Narration: the North-South Commuter Railway's Valenzuela to Malolos segment

asr-000379
00:44:40.040 --> 00:44:42.040
AVP Narration: will be operational this year.

asr-000380
00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:44.040
AVP Narration: Once fully operational,

asr-000381
00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:46.040
AVP Narration: the 147-kilometer rail line

asr-000382
00:44:46.040 --> 00:44:49.040
AVP Narration: can service 800,000 passengers daily,

asr-000383
00:44:49.040 --> 00:44:50.040
AVP Narration: reducing travel time between

asr-000384
00:44:50.040 --> 00:44:53.040
AVP Narration: Clark-Pampanga and Calamba, Laguna

asr-000385
00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:55.040
AVP Narration: from over 4 hours to just 2 hours.

asr-000386
00:44:55.040 --> 00:44:58.040
AVP Narration: Preparations for the NSCR's operations and maintenance

asr-000387
00:44:58.040 --> 00:44:59.040
AVP Narration: are underway.

asr-000388
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:04.200
AVP Narration: with the public-private partnership market sounding activities being held in different countries.

asr-000389
00:45:04.500 --> 00:45:11.960
AVP Narration: Relocation activities are also ongoing and progressing in Cavite, Laguna, and Pampanga to support communities affected by the said project.

asr-000390
00:45:12.260 --> 00:45:18.800
AVP Narration: Meanwhile, the MRT-7's first 12 stations are expected to be operational by second quarter of next year,

asr-000391
00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:23.040
AVP Narration: connecting North Avenue in Quezon City to Sacred Heart in Caloocan.

asr-000392
00:45:23.040 --> 00:45:31.720
AVP Narration: Once the project is completed, connecting Quezon City all the way to Bulacan will cut travel times from 2 to 3 hours to just 35 minutes

asr-000393
00:45:31.720 --> 00:45:35.260
AVP Narration: and can serve up to 850,000 passengers daily.

asr-000394
00:45:36.140 --> 00:45:43.480
AVP Narration: Existing rail infrastructure is also being rehabilitated to provide an improved and more convenient travel experience for commuters.

asr-000395
00:45:44.360 --> 00:45:50.380
AVP Narration: The rehabilitation of MRT-3's Quezon Avenue station offers clearer and larger wayfinding signs,

asr-000396
00:45:50.380 --> 00:45:52.760
AVP Narration: cleaner and more accessible restrooms,

asr-000397
00:45:53.140 --> 00:45:54.640
AVP Narration: wider passenger spaces,

asr-000398
00:45:55.240 --> 00:45:56.320
AVP Narration: improved ventilation,

asr-000399
00:45:57.040 --> 00:46:01.320
AVP Narration: and platform window louvers and tactile tiles for persons with visual impairment.

asr-000400
00:46:01.660 --> 00:46:04.180
AVP Narration: These upgrades are designed to make commuting easier.

asr-000401
00:46:04.820 --> 00:46:07.800
AVP Narration: As Quezon Avenue station sets the pace for improvements,

asr-000402
00:46:08.300 --> 00:46:13.620
AVP Narration: other MRT-3 stations are set to follow suit as rehabilitation works continue across the line.

asr-000403
00:46:14.420 --> 00:46:18.180
AVP Narration: At the center of Metro Manila's growing rail network is the Common Station,

asr-000404
00:46:18.180 --> 00:46:20.680
AVP Narration: or the Unified Grand Central Station.

asr-000405
00:46:21.520 --> 00:46:22.960
AVP Narration: The connecting LRT-1,

asr-000406
00:46:23.040 --> 00:46:24.040
AVP Narration: MRT-3,

asr-000407
00:46:24.040 --> 00:46:25.040
AVP Narration: and MRT-7

asr-000408
00:46:25.040 --> 00:46:30.040
AVP Narration: will ensure seamless transfers for at least 1.28 million passengers.

asr-000409
00:46:31.040 --> 00:46:33.040
AVP Narration: To the south of Manila,

asr-000410
00:46:33.040 --> 00:46:39.040
AVP Narration: the LRT-1 Cavite Extension is bringing rail service closer to Parañaque, Las Piñas, and Cavite.

asr-000411
00:46:39.040 --> 00:46:50.040
AVP Narration: The 11.7-kilometer extension with eight new stations is expected to reduce Baclaran to Bacoor travel time from around 70 minutes to only 25 minutes.

asr-000412
00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:52.040
AVP Narration: And beyond Metro Manila,

asr-000413
00:46:52.040 --> 00:46:56.040
AVP Narration: the Mindanao Railway project is set to improve the connectivity in Davao Region.

asr-000414
00:46:57.040 --> 00:47:01.040
AVP Narration: Its first phase spans 100.2 kilometers with eight stations,

asr-000415
00:47:01.040 --> 00:47:04.040
AVP Narration: covering Tagum, Davao, and Digos,

asr-000416
00:47:04.040 --> 00:47:10.040
AVP Narration: and is expected to reduce travel time between Tagum and Digos from about three hours to just one hour.

asr-000417
00:47:13.660 --> 00:47:16.660
AVP Narration: To expedite the construction of big-ticket transport projects,

asr-000418
00:47:16.660 --> 00:47:22.660
AVP Narration: the DOTR prioritizes the resolution of right-of-way issues and property acquisition for these projects.

asr-000419
00:47:22.660 --> 00:47:23.660
AVP Narration: Through its specialized right-of-way projects,

asr-000420
00:47:23.660 --> 00:47:26.660
AVP Narration: and its specialized right-of-way and site acquisition office,

asr-000421
00:47:26.660 --> 00:47:36.660
AVP Narration: the land acquisition as of July 2026 for the NSER's Malolos to Clark segment is at 90.73% from 64.93% in 2022,

asr-000422
00:47:36.660 --> 00:47:44.660
AVP Narration: while the Rail Line's Sol-East to Calamba segment is at 64.66% from 27.99% in 2024.

asr-000423
00:47:45.660 --> 00:47:52.660
AVP Narration: Meanwhile, land procurement for the Metro Manila subway is at 90.87% from 31.76% in 2022.

asr-000424
00:47:53.660 --> 00:48:01.660
AVP Narration: While the right-of-way progress for the Mindanao Railway project is currently at 15% from 0.02% in 2022.

asr-000425
00:48:05.480 --> 00:48:08.480
AVP Narration: The DOTR is modernizing the country's road transport,

asr-000426
00:48:08.480 --> 00:48:10.480
AVP Narration: from public utility vehicles,

asr-000427
00:48:10.480 --> 00:48:12.480
AVP Narration: PUV terminals and stops,

asr-000428
00:48:12.480 --> 00:48:17.480
AVP Narration: and active transport infrastructure to encourage commuters to cycle or walk to their destinations.

asr-000429
00:48:18.480 --> 00:48:23.480
AVP Narration: The Transport Agency is pushing for the Active Transport Bike-Share System and Safe Pathways program

asr-000430
00:48:23.480 --> 00:48:25.480
AVP Narration: by building safe pathways, cycleways,

asr-000431
00:48:25.480 --> 00:48:27.480
AVP Narration: and bike-share facilities.

asr-000432
00:48:27.480 --> 00:48:33.480
AVP Narration: Once completed, the 672-kilometer Davao Public Transport Modernization Project

asr-000433
00:48:33.480 --> 00:48:36.480
AVP Narration: can serve up to 800,000 passengers daily,

asr-000434
00:48:36.480 --> 00:48:42.480
AVP Narration: providing commuters with efficient bus service, modern terminals, bus stops, and shelters.

asr-000435
00:48:42.480 --> 00:48:46.480
AVP Narration: The Cebu Bus Rapid Transit is a 17-kilometer bus system,

asr-000436
00:48:46.480 --> 00:48:49.480
AVP Narration: which offers safe and efficient transport for Cebuan.

asr-000437
00:48:49.480 --> 00:48:52.480
AVP Narration: Following the completion of the three stations of Package 1,

asr-000438
00:48:52.480 --> 00:48:55.480
AVP Narration: the DOTr officially launched the Cebu BRT partial

asr-000439
00:48:55.480 --> 00:48:59.480
AVP Narration: operations on March 13, 2026

asr-000440
00:48:59.480 --> 00:49:03.480
AVP Narration: from Fuente, CNU, and CSBT stations.

asr-000441
00:49:04.480 --> 00:49:09.480
AVP Narration: The Ilocos Norte Transport Hub and Parking Building is a multi-level facility in Luwag City,

asr-000442
00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:12.480
AVP Narration: which will serve as a key transport point for commuters

asr-000443
00:49:12.480 --> 00:49:15.480
AVP Narration: traveling within and outside Ilocos Norte.

asr-000444
00:49:15.480 --> 00:49:19.480
AVP Narration: The Taguig City Integrated Terminal Exchange is a multi-model transport hub

asr-000445
00:49:19.480 --> 00:49:22.480
AVP Narration: in Arca South, Taguig City, integrating buses,

asr-000446
00:49:22.480 --> 00:49:24.480
AVP Narration: jeepneys, taxis,

asr-000447
00:49:24.480 --> 00:49:25.480
AVP Narration: the NSCR,

asr-000448
00:49:25.480 --> 00:49:27.480
AVP Narration: and the Metro Manila subway.

asr-000449
00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:34.480
AVP Narration: It is also designed to accommodate about 160,000 passengers and 5,200 PVBs daily.

asr-000450
00:49:34.480 --> 00:49:38.480
AVP Narration: The 30-kilometer EDSA busway project has provided greater ease of travel

asr-000451
00:49:38.480 --> 00:49:41.480
AVP Narration: to over 367 million passengers.

asr-000452
00:49:41.480 --> 00:49:44.480
AVP Narration: Operating 24-7 across 24 stations,

asr-000453
00:49:44.480 --> 00:49:48.480
AVP Narration: it has reduced commuter travel time from Monumento in Caloocan

asr-000454
00:49:48.480 --> 00:49:53.480
AVP Narration: to PITX in Paranaque City from 2.5 to 3 hours down to just 45 to 60 minutes.

asr-000455
00:49:54.480 --> 00:49:59.480
AVP Narration: Meanwhile, the 66.85-kilometer South Luzon Expressway Toll Road 4 project

asr-000456
00:49:59.480 --> 00:50:04.480
AVP Narration: will cut travel time from Santo Tomas, Batangas to Mayao, Quezon by three hours,

asr-000457
00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:08.480
AVP Narration: from the usual 4 hours of travel to just an hour.

asr-000458
00:50:08.480 --> 00:50:12.480
AVP Narration: Package A to C from Santo Tomas, Batangas to Tiyang, Quezon

asr-000459
00:50:12.480 --> 00:50:14.480
AVP Narration: is set to open in December,

asr-000460
00:50:14.480 --> 00:50:17.480
AVP Narration: spreading travel time from 2 hours to only 30 minutes.

asr-000461
00:50:17.480 --> 00:50:22.480
AVP Narration: President Marcus Jr. inaugurated the Cavitex C5 Link Segment 3B last March,

asr-000462
00:50:22.480 --> 00:50:27.480
AVP Narration: which aims to reduce travel time between Paranaque City and Taguig City to just 15 minutes.

asr-000463
00:50:27.480 --> 00:50:33.480
AVP Narration: The DOTr and the Toll Regulatory Board continue to advance the country's toll road infrastructure,

asr-000464
00:50:33.480 --> 00:50:39.480
AVP Narration: streamlining travel and boosting connectivity across key expressways nationwide.

asr-000465
00:50:39.480 --> 00:50:43.480
AVP Narration: President Marcus Jr. inaugurated the Naia Expressway Westbound

asr-000466
00:50:43.480 --> 00:50:47.480
AVP Narration: off-ramp to Terminal 3 on March 27, 2026,

asr-000467
00:50:47.480 --> 00:50:51.480
AVP Narration: further strengthening Naia's connectivity by offering a direct route that bypasses Conjunto.

asr-000468
00:50:52.480 --> 00:50:57.480
AVP Narration: The C5 North Link Expressway project,

asr-000469
00:50:57.480 --> 00:51:00.480
AVP Narration: Segment 8.2 to Section 1A,

asr-000470
00:51:00.480 --> 00:51:03.480
AVP Narration: targeted for inauguration in September 2026,

asr-000471
00:51:03.480 --> 00:51:08.480
AVP Narration: covers the first 2-kilometer portion of the 11.5-kilometer Segment 8.2

asr-000472
00:51:08.480 --> 00:51:12.480
AVP Narration: stretch off to CP Garcia, Katipunan, QC.

asr-000473
00:51:12.480 --> 00:51:17.480
AVP Narration: It shortens the travel time between Mindanao Avenue and Commonwealth Avenue by 35 minutes

asr-000474
00:51:17.480 --> 00:51:20.480
AVP Narration: and be there in just about 10 minutes.

asr-000475
00:51:20.480 --> 00:51:21.480
AVP Narration: President Marcos Jr. inaugurated the One RFID, All Tollways program

asr-000476
00:51:21.480 --> 00:51:28.480
AVP Narration: on October 21, 2025 at SLEX, Laguna,

asr-000477
00:51:28.480 --> 00:51:33.480
AVP Narration: which aims to make electronic and cash tall payment systems work together across expressways

asr-000478
00:51:33.480 --> 00:51:37.480
AVP Narration: for faster and more seamless travel of tall paying motorists.

asr-000479
00:51:37.480 --> 00:51:42.260
AVP Narration: Upon the orders of the President,

asr-000480
00:51:42.260 --> 00:51:46.260
AVP Narration: the DOTR is upgrading and modernizing the country's aviation infrastructure

asr-000481
00:51:46.260 --> 00:51:50.260
AVP Narration: to boost the country's economy, tourism and connectivity.

asr-000482
00:51:50.260 --> 00:51:52.260
AVP Narration: As of July 2026,

asr-000483
00:51:52.260 --> 00:51:59.720
AVP Narration: A total of 83 airport projects nationwide have been successfully completed, improving the country's connectivity and regional progress.

asr-000484
00:52:00.340 --> 00:52:06.200
AVP Narration: In the north, Laoag International Airport has undergone major expansion of its passenger terminal building,

asr-000485
00:52:06.200 --> 00:52:16.020
AVP Narration: increasing its floor space to 7,000 square meters to service wide-bodied aircraft and sit around 980 passengers from the previous 725.

asr-000486
00:52:16.020 --> 00:52:27.360
AVP Narration: In Palawan, dual development initiatives at Busuanga Airport are strengthening and extending runways up to 2,100 meters to accommodate jet operations such as A320,

asr-000487
00:52:28.100 --> 00:52:32.340
AVP Narration: paving the way for stronger tourism growth and easier air travel access.

asr-000488
00:52:33.060 --> 00:52:43.700
AVP Narration: In Albay, the Bicol International Airport's passenger terminal building and site development works are almost 100% physically finished, meeting international standards.

asr-000489
00:52:44.720 --> 00:52:46.000
AVP Narration: Meanwhile, in Western Visayas,

asr-000490
00:52:46.020 --> 00:52:56.040
AVP Narration: in Visayas, PBBM inaugurated last January the new and modernized Antique Airport with its larger passenger terminal, apron, and expanded taxiway.

asr-000491
00:52:56.660 --> 00:53:05.040
AVP Narration: In Bukidnon, the airport's new airside facilities and the 3,600-square-meter terminal are underway to serve jet aircraft operations.

asr-000492
00:53:05.520 --> 00:53:13.540
AVP Narration: Now halfway through completion, the project will seamlessly link Bukidnon and the rest of north-central Mindanao to faster, wider air travel,

asr-000493
00:53:13.540 --> 00:53:15.480
AVP Narration: opening doors for tourism,

asr-000494
00:53:16.020 --> 00:53:16.500
AVP Narration: trade,

asr-000495
00:53:16.500 --> 00:53:18.120
AVP Narration: and new investment in the region.

asr-000496
00:53:18.700 --> 00:53:29.160
AVP Narration: Davao International Airport's expansion includes an 8,400 m2 of terminal space to accommodate up to 2,200 domestic and international passengers.

asr-000497
00:53:29.160 --> 00:53:40.640
AVP Narration: In the country's surfing capital, Siargao, the Siargao airport is expanding its terminal through a modular facility, increasing its seating capacity to 573 and additional check-in counters.

asr-000498
00:53:41.500 --> 00:53:45.560
AVP Narration: Public-private partnerships are also enabling fast track progress and various projects.

asr-000499
00:53:46.020 --> 00:53:48.220
AVP Narration: seamless international and regional travel.

asr-000500
00:53:48.720 --> 00:53:54.240
AVP Narration: At the country's primary gateway, the Ninoy Aquino International Airport underwent major transformation

asr-000501
00:53:54.240 --> 00:53:57.380
AVP Narration: following its turnover to new Naia InfraCorp.

asr-000502
00:53:57.380 --> 00:54:03.640
AVP Narration: Under the NNIC, Naia's annual passenger capacity has doubled from 35 to 62 million.

asr-000503
00:54:04.480 --> 00:54:10.640
AVP Narration: Last December 2025, the President inaugurated the new modern facilities at Naia Terminal 3,

asr-000504
00:54:10.640 --> 00:54:16.500
AVP Narration: activating 78 biometric immigration e-gates, launching the Dignitaries Lounge,

asr-000505
00:54:16.900 --> 00:54:21.620
AVP Narration: and opening the Tambayan and Mazanin food halls for a world-class passenger experience.

asr-000506
00:54:22.080 --> 00:54:26.440
AVP Narration: Following the handover of the Laguindingan Airport to Aboiti's InfraCapital,

asr-000507
00:54:26.880 --> 00:54:33.460
AVP Narration: the airport's current annual passenger capacity of 1.6 million is expected to increase to 3.9 million,

asr-000508
00:54:33.940 --> 00:54:39.760
AVP Narration: with improvements of its airport facilities now underway for long-term efficiency and passenger demand.

asr-000509
00:54:39.760 --> 00:54:44.640
AVP Narration: The ongoing terminal reconfiguration of the Bohol Panglao International Airport

asr-000510
00:54:44.640 --> 00:54:48.140
AVP Narration: will scale up its capacity to 2.5 million passengers,

asr-000511
00:54:48.280 --> 00:54:52.720
AVP Narration: while a new passenger terminal building will increase its further to 3.9 million.

asr-000512
00:54:57.000 --> 00:55:02.040
AVP Narration: Inter-island connectivity has vastly improved as the DOTR and the Philippine Ports Authority

asr-000513
00:55:02.040 --> 00:55:06.640
AVP Narration: continue to modernize the ports to provide efficient movement of people and goods.

asr-000514
00:55:06.920 --> 00:55:11.020
AVP Narration: The Philippine Ports Authority has completed 15 port projects in 2025

asr-000515
00:55:11.020 --> 00:55:13.400
AVP Narration: and six port projects as of June 2026.

asr-000516
00:55:13.440 --> 00:55:20.540
AVP Narration: On April 22, 2025, the President inaugurated the new fourth operations building

asr-000517
00:55:20.540 --> 00:55:26.220
AVP Narration: of the Balingoan Port in Misamis Oriental, increasing its passenger capacity to 500 from

asr-000518
00:55:26.220 --> 00:55:32.880
AVP Narration: the previous 150. The President also unveiled on December 12, 2025, the new Banago Port in

asr-000519
00:55:32.880 --> 00:55:39.360
AVP Narration: Negros Occidental. The port can now accommodate 500 passengers from its previous 50 passengers.

asr-000520
00:55:39.360 --> 00:55:43.360
AVP Narration: On July 13, 2026, the President inaugurated the new

asr-000521
00:55:43.440 --> 00:55:48.720
AVP Narration: Benoni Ports Passenger Terminal Building and Benoni Port Lifecraft Landing Station,

asr-000522
00:55:48.720 --> 00:55:51.520
AVP Narration: which is seen to boost Camiguin's tourism.

asr-000523
00:55:51.520 --> 00:55:57.600
AVP Narration: On July 21, 2026, the President led the inspection of the new and modernized passenger terminal

asr-000524
00:55:57.600 --> 00:56:04.480
AVP Narration: building of the Port of Lucena. The Lucena Port PTV has increased its sitting capacity to 967

asr-000525
00:56:04.480 --> 00:56:10.640
AVP Narration: from its previous 607. This significantly benefits the province as the port can now

asr-000526
00:56:10.640 --> 00:56:13.120
AVP Narration: accommodate more tourists and passengers,

asr-000527
00:56:13.120 --> 00:56:15.920
AVP Narration: providing them with comfortable travel experience.

asr-000528
00:56:15.920 --> 00:56:20.720
AVP Narration: The PPA has also completed various port projects in different provinces in Luzon,

asr-000529
00:56:20.720 --> 00:56:28.080
AVP Narration: Visayas, and Mindanao. As of June 25, 2026, 87 PPA port projects are ongoing,

asr-000530
00:56:28.080 --> 00:56:33.440
AVP Narration: 33 projects in Luzon, 33 in Visayas, and 21 in Mindanao.

asr-000531
00:56:36.390 --> 00:56:41.350
AVP Narration: In April 2025, the Coast Guard District in the Kalayaan Island Group was officially

asr-000532
00:56:41.350 --> 00:56:45.030
AVP Narration: activated to assert the country's sovereignty and enforce maritime laws.

asr-000533
00:56:45.750 --> 00:56:50.150
AVP Narration: The mandate of the newly activated Coast Guard District in the Kalayaan Island Group is to

asr-000534
00:56:50.150 --> 00:56:55.270
AVP Narration: perform maritime security, enforce Philippine maritime laws, and assert the country's

asr-000535
00:56:55.270 --> 00:57:04.680
AVP Narration: sovereignty in the West Philippine Sea. Meanwhile, the PCG continues to carry out

asr-000536
00:57:04.680 --> 00:57:11.000
AVP Narration: rescue operations and relief efforts, safeguarding millions of holiday travelers, rescuing thousands

asr-000537
00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:17.160
AVP Narration: of Filipinos at sea, and evacuating hundreds of thousands ahead of back-to-back Super Typhoons.

asr-000540
00:57:19.060 --> 00:57:24.760
AVP Narration: Beyond delivering big-ticket infrastructure projects, the DOTr remains committed to ensuring that every peso

asr-000541
00:57:24.760 --> 00:57:29.840
AVP Narration: of its budget is responsibly and efficiently spent for the benefit of the Filipino people.

asr-000542
00:57:30.660 --> 00:57:36.100
AVP Narration: The commitment was affirmed when, for the first time in over three decades, the DOTR

asr-000543
00:57:36.100 --> 00:57:41.920
AVP Narration: received an unmodified opinion from the Commission on Audit for Fiscal Year 2025, reflecting

asr-000544
00:57:41.920 --> 00:57:46.840
AVP Narration: the agency's compliance with applicable financial reporting standards and proper stewardship

asr-000545
00:57:46.840 --> 00:57:48.000
AVP Narration: of public funds.

asr-000546
00:57:48.000 --> 00:57:53.320
AVP Narration: These accomplishments in the transportation sector have opened up a broader spectrum of

asr-000547
00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:58.140
AVP Narration: opportunities for the country's development, helping strengthen the economy and support

asr-000548
00:57:58.140 --> 00:57:59.060
AVP Narration: long-term growth.

asr-000549
00:57:59.660 --> 00:58:05.320
AVP Narration: By addressing bottlenecks and gaps in transportation infrastructure, the DOTR remains steadfast

asr-000550
00:58:05.320 --> 00:58:10.420
AVP Narration: in its trust and long-term vision of improving mobility and strengthening connectivity across

asr-000551
00:58:10.420 --> 00:58:11.380
AVP Narration: the archipelago.

asr-000552
00:58:11.800 --> 00:58:16.880
AVP Narration: With several projects set for completion, the President assures Filipinos of its chief

asr-000553
00:58:16.880 --> 00:58:17.260
AVP Narration: goal.

asr-000554
00:58:17.260 --> 00:58:20.240
AVP Narration: To make their daily commute convenient and comfortable.

asr-000555
00:58:37.970 --> 00:58:38.950
